# Docker reads .dockerignore from the BUILD CONTEXT root, not the repo root. This service
# builds with `context: src/AiObservatory.Web` (see docker-compose.yml), so the repo-root
# .dockerignore — which does exclude **/node_modules — is never consulted for this image.
# Without this file `COPY . .` copies the host's node_modules straight over the clean
# `npm ci` from the layer above, replacing Linux binaries with Windows ones. Vite then
# loads a mismatched rolldown native binding and the build dies with
# `value "builtin:vite-wasm-fallback" does not match any variant of enum
# BindingBuiltinPluginName`.
#
# It only bites locally: CI builds from a clean checkout with no node_modules on disk,
# so "Frontend (UI)" stays green while `docker compose build web` fails.
node_modules

# Build output — stale, and regenerated inside the image anyway.
dist

# Local secrets only — the same three patterns the repo-root .dockerignore uses, kept
# deliberately narrow. A blanket `.env.*` would also drop a committed `.env.production`,
# which Vite reads at build time; the Dockerfile already neutralises that file by blanking
# the VITE_* vars on the build command, and process env beats a .env file in Vite. Dropping
# it here as well would silently discard any non-VITE_ var someone later expects to be baked in.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Local noise that has no business in a build context.
.vite
coverage
*.log
.DS_Store
